    <div class="legal-section" id="subscriptions">
      <span class="legal-num">01</span>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Access &amp; Subscription Terms</h2>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <p>By creating an account or subscribing to the Jorgensen Foundation platform, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. Academic access is provided free of charge to eligible researchers (see below). Industry subscriptions are offered on a monthly or annual basis. Both grant access to the platform's computational chemistry programs, cloud computing resources, and associated tools for the duration of your account or active subscription period.</p>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Academic Access (Free)</h3>
        <p>Academic access is provided free of charge to individuals affiliated with accredited universities, colleges, and non-profit research institutes. Your eligibility is determined automatically by your email domain at the time of registration. If your institution uses a non-standard domain, you must provide verification of your affiliation before free academic access is granted. Free academic access includes full use of the platform's programs and cloud computing resources and requires no payment or payment method. Free academic access is sustained by revenue from industry subscriptions, and the Foundation may revise its scope on reasonable notice.</p>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Industry Subscriptions</h3>
        <p>Industry pricing applies to all subscribers who do not qualify for free academic access. Industry subscriptions are priced at $199 per month (monthly plan) or $1,990 per year (annual plan). Industry subscribers receive priority queue access, a dedicated technical support contact, and API access for integration with internal pipelines in addition to all features included in the free academic tier.</p>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Billing</h3>
        <p>Billing applies to industry subscriptions only; academic accounts are free and require no payment method. Industry subscriptions are billed in advance — monthly subscriptions on the same day each month, annual subscriptions once per year on the anniversary of the subscription start date. Payment is processed by Stripe. By subscribing, you authorise the Jorgensen Foundation to charge your payment method on the applicable billing cycle. All prices are in US dollars and exclusive of any applicable taxes, which are your responsibility.</p>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Account Sharing</h3>
        <p>Each account is for a single named user. Sharing login credentials or allowing multiple individuals to access the platform under a single account is not permitted. Organisations requiring access for multiple users should contact us to discuss multi-seat arrangements.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="cancellation">
      <span class="legal-num">02</span>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Cancellation and Refund Policy</h2>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <p>You may cancel your subscription at any time from your account settings. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period — you retain full access to the platform until that date.</p>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Monthly Subscriptions</h3>
        <p>If you cancel a monthly subscription, your access continues until the end of the current monthly billing period. No partial-month refunds are issued. Your saved data, simulation inputs, and results remain accessible for 90 days after cancellation, after which they are permanently deleted.</p>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Annual Subscriptions</h3>
        <p>If you cancel an annual subscription, your access continues until the end of the current annual term. We do not offer partial-year refunds on annual subscriptions. If you believe your circumstances warrant an exception, please contact us at info@jorgensenfoundation.org and we will consider your request at our discretion.</p>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Refunds</h3>
        <p>Refunds are not issued for unused subscription periods except where required by applicable consumer protection law. If you experience a technical failure that prevents you from using the platform for a sustained period and you have notified us promptly, we may issue a pro-rated credit at our discretion. We do not issue refunds for dissatisfaction with simulation results, as the accuracy of computational results depends on inputs and parameters outside our control.</p>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Foundation-Initiated Termination</h3>
        <p>We reserve the right to suspend or terminate your account without notice if you violate these Terms of Service, in particular the Acceptable Use provisions in Section 3. In the event of termination for cause, no refund will be issued.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="acceptable-use">
      <span class="legal-num">03</span>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Acceptable Use of Programs</h2>
      <div class="legal-body">
        <p>The Jorgensen Foundation platform provides access to scientific simulation software for legitimate research, educational, and commercial purposes in computational chemistry and related fields. By using the platform, you agree to the following acceptable use conditions.</p>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Permitted Uses</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Academic research, teaching, and scientific publication</li>
          <li>Commercial drug discovery, materials science, and related research and development</li>
          <li>Method development and benchmarking in computational chemistry</li>
          <li>Training and educational use within the subscriber's institution</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Prohibited Uses</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Attempting to reverse engineer, decompile, or extract the source code of any program</li>
          <li>Automated scraping, bulk downloading, or harvesting of platform data beyond normal simulation workflows</li>
          <li>Using the platform to develop competing simulation software or to reproduce the programs outside the platform</li>
          <li>Sharing access credentials with third parties or allowing unauthorised users to access your account</li>
          <li>Submitting malicious inputs designed to disrupt, exploit, or compromise platform infrastructure</li>
          <li>Using computing resources for purposes unrelated to the platform's intended simulation workflows</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="legal-h3">Publications and Attribution</h3>
        <p>If you publish research that uses the Jorgensen Foundation programs, you must cite the relevant primary references as specified on each program's page. You may acknowledge use of the Jorgensen Foundation cloud platform in your methods section but are not required to do so. You may not represent the programs as your own software or omit attribution in a manner that misleads readers about the origin of the computational methods used.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

